# ============================================================================
# File: 02_analyze_extreme_event_case_crossover_simulation.R
# Purpose:
#   Analyze simulation data generated by
#   01_generate_extreme_event_case_crossover_simulation.R and compare four
#   estimators of the additional extreme-event-history log mortality rate ratio.
#
# Estimators:
#   1. Conventional conditional logistic regression.
#   2. Outcome-model estimating-equation estimator (f = 0).
#   3. Exposure-regression estimating-equation estimator (g = 0).
#   4. Proposed generalized AIPW estimator.
#
# Primary performance metrics:
#   - Scenario-specific absolute empirical coefficient bias.
#   - Overall mean absolute coefficient bias across the three scenarios in
#     which at least one nuisance model is correctly specified.
#   - Worst-case absolute coefficient bias across those three scenarios.
#   - Overall mean absolute bias of the mean annual attributable fraction.
#   - Mean empirical 95% confidence interval coverage.
#   - Numerical convergence rate.
#
# Fixed project path:
#   /xxx/ccc
#
# Optional environment variables:
#   EXTREME_ANALYSIS_WORKERS         = parallel workers; default 1
#   EXTREME_ANALYSIS_OVERWRITE       = TRUE/FALSE; default FALSE
#   EXTREME_ANALYSIS_MAX_REPLICATES  = maximum replicates per scenario;
#                                      0 means use all available replicates
#   EXTREME_XGB_THREADS              = XGBoost threads per model; default 1
# ============================================================================

options(stringsAsFactors = FALSE)

